icence</h1></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ccl-banner-top-container"><div class="ccl-container"> <nav class="ccl-breadcrumb ccl-banner-top-bar-paragraph breadcrumb-container" aria-label="breadcrumb"><div class="ccl-banner-top-bar-left"> <nav class="ccl-breadcrumb" role="navigation" aria-labelledby="system-breadcrumb"><h2 id="system-breadcrumb" class="visually-hidden">Breadcrumb</h2> <span class="ccl-u-sr-only">You are here:</span><ol class="ccl-breadcrumb__segments-wrapper"><li class="ccl-breadcrumb__segment ccl-breadcrumb__segment--first "> <a href="/" class="ccl-link ccl-link--inverted ccl-link--standalone ccl-breadcrumb__link">Home</a></li><li class="ccl-breadcrumb__segment "> <a href="/user-corner/" class="ccl-link ccl-link--inverted ccl-link--standalone ccl-breadcrumb__link">User Corner</a></li><li class="ccl-breadcrumb__segment ccl-breadcrumb__segment--last "> Service Commitments and License</li></ol> </nav></div> </nav></div></div></div><div class="spacer__twenty"></div><div class="ccl-container"><div class="row"><div class="col-sm-hide col-md-hide col-mdx-4 col-lg-3 col-xl-3"><div class="field field--field_sidebar_block field--name-field-sidebar-block field--type-entity-reference-revisions field--label-hidden"><div><div class="field__item"><div class="paragraph paragraph--type--block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--field_block_entity field--name-field-block-entity field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div id="block-menuitemblock" data-block-plugin-id="menu_item_block" class="settings-tray-editable block block-marine-block block-menu-item-block" data-drupal-settingstray="editable"><ul class="ccl-header-main-menu menu"><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/user-corner/getting-started" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/393">Getting started</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item--collapsed"> <a href="/services/user-learning-services/tutorials" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/4662">E-learning materials</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="https://help.marine.copernicus.eu/en/" target="_blank">Help Center &amp; FAQ</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/user-corner/user-notification-service" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/54">User notification service</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/user-corner/feedback" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/23179">Feedback</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="https://pqd.mercator-ocean.fr/" target="_blank">Product Quality</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item--collapsed"> <a href="/user-corner/product-roadmap/transition-information" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/18945">Product Roadmap</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/services/use-cases/" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/46">Get Inspired</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/user-corner/service-commitments-and-licence" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/421" class="is-active" aria-current="page">Service Commitments and Licence</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/contact" target="_self" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/4570">Contact Us</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-mdx-8 col-lg-9 col-xl-9"><div class="node__content"><div class="table-of-contents visually-hidden white-style"><div class="container" id="container-toc"> <a class="btn btn-primary" data-bs-toggle="collapse" href="#toc" role="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="toc"><h2>Summary</h2> </a><div id="toc" class="collapse in"></div></div></div><div class="node-page-field-content"><div class="field field--field_content field--name-field-content field--type-entity-reference-revisions field--label-hidden"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row field__items"><div class="col-12 field__item"><div class="paragraph paragraph--type--container paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="ccl-container "><div data-contextual-id="paragraph:root_parent_type=node&amp;root_parent=421&amp;paragraph=8118:changed=1727952283&amp;langcode=en" data-contextual-token="D1J9N44KMw8RmQZMrn4rqbg9Pt4SjFep5nnUR7GXluM" data-drupal-ajax-container=""></div><div class="field field--field_container_content field--name-field-container-content field--type-entity-reference-revisions field--label-hidden"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row field__items"><div class="col-12 field__item"><div class="paragraph paragraph--type--formatted-text paragraph--view-mode--default"><div data-contextual-id="paragraph:root_parent_type=node&amp;root_parent=421&amp;paragraph=8117:changed=1727952283&amp;langcode=en" data-contextual-token="5jDsgTmXGRoyNh_oiuOxmKmFCA8zqznuxxQlxg9dWiM" data-drupal-ajax-container=""></div><div class="field field--field_formatted_text field--name-field-formatted-text field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"><p>In this <strong>Service Level Agreement</strong> (SLA), using the acronym “<strong>CMEMS</strong>” or the shortened name “<strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong>” both denote the E.U. <strong>Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service</strong>.</p><h2 class="ccl-heading--h2">1. Preamble</h2><p>This document is integral part of the “Service Level Agreement” (SLA) or “Agreement” between the <strong>User</strong> and <strong>the Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service</strong> for the provision of the Copernicus Marine services. Its purpose is to outline the range and level of services that the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> will supply to the <strong>User</strong>.</p><p><strong>Before signing the SLA, the User is informed of the commitments on service (paragraph 2) and conditions of use described in the CMEMS licence (Annex).</strong></p><p>This SLA concerns the operational phase of the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service </strong>from<strong> November 2023.</strong></p><p>All the products are accessible directly from the Web Portal portal: a centralised access with a single password, thus all of them are monitored by the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> and then allow an homogenous level of service.</p><p>The SLA will be updated in the event of changes in service commitments.</p><h2 class="ccl-heading--h2">2. CMEMS commitments on service</h2><table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><p>The CMEMS <strong>User Support</strong> is the single point of contact for CMEMS <strong>Users</strong> for all issues relating to the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong>. It can be reached&nbsp;on the CMEMS web portal by login to the "chat", located at the bottom right, the "help center" or the "online tutorials" available on the <a href="https://marine.copernicus.eu/contact" title="Contact Us page">Contact Us</a> page.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.1 Service Elements: Copernicus Marine Service information</strong></em></h3><h3>2.1.1 Oceanographics products</h3><p>All products are detailed in the Copernicus Marine Service <a href="https://data.marine.copernicus.eu/products" title="CMEMS Products Catalogue">catalogue</a>. They are 3 kinds:</p><ul><li><strong>Forecas</strong>t (Model Outputs)</li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Near Real time Products </strong>(Model Outputs and Observations)</p></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Multi Year Products</strong><br>Hindcast and Re-analysis of Model Outputs<br>Reprocessing of Observations</li></ul><p>They cover the 7 following geographical areas:</p><ul><li>Global Ocean</li><li>Arctic Ocean</li><li>Baltic Sea</li><li>Atlantic North West Shelf Seas</li><li>Iberia Biscay Ireland Regional Seas</li><li>Mediterranean Sea</li><li>Black Sea</li></ul><p>And contain the following parameters:</p><ul><li>Temperature</li><li>Salinity</li><li>Sea Surface Height</li><li>Current Velocity</li><li>Mixed Layer Thickness</li><li>Sea Ice</li><li>Wind</li><li>Sea Surface Wave</li><li>Plankton</li><li>Oxygen</li><li>Nutrients</li><li>Carbon</li><li>Primary Production</li><li>Reflectance</li><li>Turbidity</li><li>Transparency</li></ul><p>The products of the catalogue are available in an electronic form, accessible via the on-line catalogue (by the web portal or by executable scripts).</p><p>The ocean maps for the products in the catalogue are provided in the <a href="https://data.marine.copernicus.eu/viewer/expert?view=viewer&amp;crs=epsg%3A4326&amp;t=1672747200000&amp;z=0&amp;center=0%2C5&amp;zoom=9.55&amp;layers=W3siaWQiOiJjMCIsImxheWVySWQiOiJHTE9CQUxfQU5BTFlTSVNfRk9SRUNBU1RfQklPXzAwMV8wMjgvZ2xvYmFsLWFuYWx5c2lzLWZvcmVjYXN0LWJpby0wMDEtMDI4LWRhaWx5L2NobCIsInpJbmRleCI6MCwibG9nU2NhbGUiOnRydWV9XQ%3D%3D">MyOcean viewer</a></p><h3>2.1.2 Ocean Monitoring Indicators</h3><p>Based on this product catalogue, key reference information on the state of the ocean is provided in the <strong>Ocean Monitoring Indicators</strong> (<a href="https://marine.copernicus.eu/access-data/ocean-monitoring-indicators">OMIs) catalogue</a>. The monitoring indicators are:</p><ul class="ccl-list"><li><u>Ocean Climate</u>: Sea surface temperature, Ocean heat uptake, Ocean carbon uptake, Sea level mean, Sea ice change, Ocean freshwater;</li><li><u>Ocean Health</u>: Chlorophyll &amp; primary production, Ocean acidification, Ocean deoxygenation, Eutrophication &amp; blooms, Oligotrophication, Coral health;</li><li><u>Ocean Circulation</u>: Ocean heat transport, Ocean volume transport, Meridional overturning circulation, Ocean gyres &amp; upwelling, Boundary currents, Wind driven circulation;</li><li><u>Ocean Variability and Extremes</u>: Marine heat waves, Cold spells, Climate variability, Extreme sea level, Sea state, Storm and cyclone potential.</li></ul><h3>2.1.3 Ocean State Report</h3><p>Comprehensive and state-of-the-art assessment of the state of the global ocean and European regional seas is provided in the <a href="https://marine.copernicus.eu/access-data/ocean-state-report" title="Ocean State Report">Ocean State Report</a>.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.2 Additional products from another service provider available through the Copernicus Marine Service</strong></em></h3><p>Some SeaDataNet, EUMETSAT/OSI SAF, GHRSST, EMODnet, C3S and ESA-CCI products are distributed by the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong>. The relevant credits are mentionned in the product documentation.</p><p>These products are therefore in two different catalogues.</p><p>In the event of unavailability or delay of these products by their original service provider to CMEMS, the <strong>Corpernicus Marine Service</strong> will not be held responsible for any interruption of supply to the <strong>User</strong>.</p><p>The <strong>CMEMS</strong> level of monitoring of these products is the same as the other products within the Copernicus Marine Service catalogue.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.3 Web portal</strong></em></h3><p>The <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> web portal is the main entry point to access the CMEMS Products &amp; Services.</p><p>The <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> commitments on this service element are as follows:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - The availability of access to the CMEMS web portal is 97% over a year (percentage of days without failure per year).</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - The download of products by on-line catalogue is available to users as soon as the products are produced.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; For the near real-time products, a target delivery time is defined in the associated Product User Manual.</p><p>*Days are from Monday to Friday, excluding public holidays.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong><a name="sd_commitments"></a>2.4 User Support</strong></em></h3><p>The <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> commitments on the User Support are as follows:</p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Information to User request is provided within 5 days over 90 % of time.<h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.5 Agreed </strong>User Support</em><em><strong> hours</strong></em></h3><p>Normal working hours are defined as 09:00-&gt;17:00 French local time from Monday to Friday, excluding French public holidays.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong><a name="2.7"></a>2.6 Confidentiality</strong></em></h3><p>Each <strong>User </strong>enquiry will be treated as commercially confidential by the Copernicus Marine Service.</p><p><strong>User</strong> details will not be transmitted outside the Copernicus Marine Service in application of the Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and of The Council of 27 April 2016 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data and on the free movement of such data, and repealing Directive&nbsp;95/46/EC (General Data Protection Regulation).</p><p>The basic principles carried by the GDPR are thus guaranteed to the <strong>User</strong>, in particular on consent for the use of personal data, the right to be forgotten, and the right to the portability of data.</p><p>Personal data collected such as family name and first name are linked to the generation of the login; The password is encrypted and invisible by the Copernicus Marine Service. Other information with regard to the organisation or how will be used products are for internal statistics purpose exclusively.</p><p><strong>User</strong> has a right of access and correction of his/her personal data, by accessing “My Account”, website part which is available in the products catalogue “Ocean Products”. Also, all requested modifications of the personal data will be done, if the <strong>User</strong> sends an email request to the User Support.</p><p>In addition to the exchange of information related to the service, the email address of the <strong>User</strong> is collected for the distribution of the Copernicus Marine Service newsletter. The <strong>User</strong> may withdraw at any time his/her consent to receive the newsletter by clicking at the bottom of the newsletter footer.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.7 Delivery of products</strong></em></h3><p>As soon as the SLA is sent to the User Support, the <strong>User</strong> is informed and receives a login and password to access to products.</p><p>Login and password are personal to the signatory of the SLA and non-transferable.</p><p>The service relies on on-line catalogue for all products.</p><p>The <strong>Use</strong><strong>r</strong> is informed about the opening of the service directly by an automatic activation e-mail.</p><p>In case of a failure in the provision of any product, updated information with an indication of the status of the incident will be posted on the web portal under the “User Notification Service”.<br>Furthermore, the <b>User</b> can subscribe to customisable RSS (Really Simple Syndication) feeds information.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.8 Service maintenance</strong></em></h3><p>The commitments on service continuity are those currently applied by the centralised information system for all the products.</p><p>Using the “User Notification Service” as described in paragraph 2.8 here above, the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> will take reasonable endeavours to provide advanced notice to <strong>Users</strong> in case of:</p><ul><li>Changes to the provision of services provided under this SLA.</li><li>Scheduled routine maintenance leading to the temporary unavailability of the services provided under this SLA.</li></ul><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.9 Service level reporting</strong></em></h3><p>The User Support will record statistics on User Support response times to allow the measurement of the service level performance against this SLA. To do this, the User Support may contact the <strong>User</strong> to request some information.</p><h3 class="ccl-heading--h3"><em><strong>2.10 User feedback</strong></em></h3><p>When registering to the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong>, the <strong>User</strong> is asked to give information about his applications and his own service, when appropriate. This information will be used to globally monitor the service and will be treated as confidential by the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service </strong>as stated in paragraph 2.7.</p><p>Moreover, in order to allow the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> to continuously improve the service, <strong>Users</strong> will be asked to give feedback on:</p><ul><li><strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> products &amp; services overall quality,</li><li>how well the products and services are relevant for the <strong>User</strong> application(s),</li><li>what further improvements can be made to the products and services.</li></ul><p>The <strong>User</strong> will make such feedbacks available to the <strong>Copernicus Marine Service</strong> upon reasonable notice being given. These feedbacks will be asked through 2 channels:</p><ul><li>a short satisfaction enquiry (regular after each exchange with the User Support),</li><li>periodic questionnaires.</li></ul><h2 class="ccl-heading--h2">3. Conditions</h2><p>All the costs (production and service) are fully covered by the <strong>Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service</strong> as provided for in the Copernicus Regulation* until the end of the <strong>Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service </strong>(planned on 30 June 2028). Thus, the <strong>Copernicus Marine Services</strong> and products are free of charge for the <strong>User </strong>until this date.</p><p>Technical upgrades and service commitment updates will be done on regular basis.</p><h2 class="ccl-heading--h2">4. Validity, duration</h2><p>This SLA shall come into force on the date of opening of the service to the <strong>User</strong> and will remain valid until the end of the<strong> Copernicus Marine Service</strong>.</p><p>(*) The EU Regulation (EU) 2021/696 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 April 2021 establishing the Union Space Programme and the European Union Agency for the Space Programme and repealing Regulations<b> </b>(EU) No 912/2010, (EU) No 1285/2013 and (EU) No 377/2014 and Decision No 541/2014/EU (OJ L 170, 12.5.2021, p.69-148).</p><h4 class="ccl-heading--h4">N.B.: note that <strong>the User is called “Licensee”</strong> in the Licence here after.</h4><p>&nbsp;<a name="licence"></a></p><h2 class="ccl-heading--h2">ANNEX</h2><h2 class="ccl-heading--h2">LICENCE TO USE THE COPERNICUS MARINE SERVICE PRODUCTS</h2><p class="text-justify">IMPORTANT NOTICE: PLEASE READ CAREFULLY BEFORE USING COPERNICUS MARINE SERVICE PRODUCTS. This Licence Agreement is a legal agreement between the Licensee and MERCATOR OCEAN and sets out the terms for use of the Copernicus Marine Service Products and information which will apply to the Licensee. Use of the Copernicus Marine Service Products means that the Licensee agrees to abide by all of the terms and conditions in this Licence.</p><h2><em><strong>Introduction</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify">(i) The Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service is funded since 2014 under the Regulation (EU) N°377/2014 of the European Parliament and of the&nbsp;Council of 3 April 2014 establishing the Copernicus Programme and then, under the EU Regulation (EU) 2021/696 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 April 2021 establishing the Union Space Programme and the European Union Agency for the Space Programme.</p><p class="text-justify">(ii) The legal entity entrusted by the Delegation Agreement signed on 11<sup>th</sup> November 2014 to implement the Copernicus Marine Environment&nbsp;Monitoring Service is <strong>MERCATOR OCEAN, </strong>renewed by the European Commission within the Contribution Agreement signed on 22<sup>nd</sup> July 2021 as the entrusted entity to implement the Copernicus component of the space programme of the European Union for the Copernicus Marine Service.</p><p>(iii) The Copernicus Marine Service Products are products listed in the Copernicus Marine Service catalogue, maintained by MERCATOR OCEAN.</p><h2><em><strong>1.Interpretation and Definitions</strong></em></h2><table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" width="650"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service</span></td><td class="text-justify" style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means the Copernicus Marine Service operation under the terms of the Regulation (EU) N° 377/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 3 April 2014 establishing the Copernicus Programme and </span>the EU Regulation (EU) 2021/696 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 April 2021 establishing the Union Space Programme and the European Union Agency for the Space Programme<span style="color: #000000;">;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Copernicus Marine Service Product(s)</span></td><td class="text-justify" style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means those products created by the Copernicus Marine Service made available for use under the Copernicus Marine Service catalogue;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Copernicus Marine Service Catalogue</span></td><td class="text-justify" style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means the list of Copernicus Marine Service Products made available via the Copernicus Marine Service website to the Licensee at any given time;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><p><span style="color: #000000;">Derivative Work</span></p></td><td class="text-justify" style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means any product and/or information which has been derived, developed and irreversibly modified from Copernicus Marine Service Product(s) or Value Added Product(s) and does not retain the original pixel structure of a Copernicus Marine Service Product;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;">Digital Object Identifiers</td><td class="text-justify" style="width: 1102px;">means persistent and stable references for scientific data, and enable data for each Copernicus Marine Product to be easily and reliably found, used and cited.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Copernicus Marine Service Information</span></td><td class="text-justify" style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means any drawings, reports, papers, or any other technical information, know-how, products, data or documents of any king, including oral information available from the Copernicus Marine Service website or issued from any Copernicus Marine Service events.</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><p><span style="color: #000000;">Intellectual Property Rights</span></p></td><td style="width: 1102px;"><p><span style="color: #000000;">intellectual property rights of all kinds regardless of the form or medium stored, including:</span></p><p><span style="color: #000000;">•all patents<br>•rights to inventions<br>•copyright and related rights<br>•moral rights<br>•trade marks and service marks<br>•trade names and domain names<br>•rights in get-up<br>•rights to goodwill or to sue for passing off or unfair competition<br>•rights in designs<br>•rights in computer software<br>•database rights<br>•rights in confidential information (including know-how and trade secrets)<br>•any other rights in the nature of intellectual property rights</span></p><p><span style="color: #000000;">in each case whether registered or unregistered and including all applications (or rights to apply) for, and renewals or extensions of, such rights and all similar or equivalent rights or forms of protection which subsist or will subsist now or in the future in any part of the world together with all rights of action in relation to the infringement of any of the above;</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Licence</span></td><td style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means the terms and conditions of this licence as amended from time to time;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Licensee</span></td><td style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means the individual or organisation which, subject to the terms and conditions of this Licence, is permitted to use the Copernicus Marine Service Products;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><p><span style="color: #000000;">Redistribution of CMEMS Product(s) and document(s)</span></p></td><td style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means any Copernicus Marine Service Product and document for which neither format nor the data have been modified, redistributed by the Licensee, under the original outcome Copernicus Marine Service catalogue name or under a new name;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">The public or third party</span></td><td style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means individual or organisation, obtaining and using the Copernicus Marine Service products disseminated by the Licensee;</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 249px;"><span style="color: #000000;">Value Added Product</span></td><td style="width: 1102px;"><span style="color: #000000;">means a product which has been created by the licensee by modifying a Copernicus Marine Service Product to a higher processing level which retains the original source image data and pixel structure;</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h2><em><strong>2. Licence Permissions</strong></em></h2><p><strong>2.1</strong> This Licence is granted free of charge.</p><p><strong>2.2</strong> The Licensee is hereby granted a worldwide, non exclusive, royalty free, perpetual licence, (subject to the terms and conditions of this&nbsp;agreement) to:</p><p>(a) make and use such reasonable copies of Copernicus Marine Service Products for internal use and back up purposes;</p><p>(b) modify, adapt, develop, create and distribute Value Added Products or Derivative Work from Copernicus Marine Service Products for any&nbsp;purpose;</p><p>(c) redistribute, disseminate any Copernicus Marine Service Product in their original form via any media.</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>2.3</strong> In application of the Regulation (EU) n° 1159/2013 of the 12 July 2013 supplementing Regulation (EU) n° 911/2010 of the European Parliament&nbsp;and of the Council on the European Earth monitoring programme, the Licensee will communicate to the public the source of the products and services by crediting the Copernicus Marine Environment&nbsp;Monitoring Service;</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>2.4</strong> <strong>Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service Credits</strong> shall be clearly visible on the home page of the Licensee’s website or at least&nbsp;on the page allowing to access to the products, in the recommended form below:</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>(a)</strong> The Licensee will ensure that value added products or derivative works developed from Copernicus Marine Service Products including&nbsp;pictures – shall credit the Copernicus Marine Service by explicitly making mention of the originator (Copernicus Marine Environment&nbsp;Monitoring Service) and by citing the DOIs in the following manner:&nbsp;</p><p class="text-center"><strong>“Generated using E.U. Copernicus Marine Service Information; </strong>insert <strong>DOIs links here”</strong><br>(whenever possible in case of long list of DOIs)</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>(b) </strong>The Licensee will ensure that in case of redistribution of Copernicus Marine Service products or documents, including pictures –&nbsp;shall credit the Copernicus Marine Service by explicitly making mention of the originator (Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring&nbsp;Service)&nbsp;and by citing the DOIs in the following manner:</p><p class="text-center"><strong>“E.U. Copernicus Marine Service Information; </strong>insert <strong>DOIs links here”</strong><br>(whenever possible in case of long list of DOIs)</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>(c)</strong> In case of any publication, the Licensee will ensure credit the Copernicus Marine Service&nbsp;and cite the DOIs links guaranteeing the traceability of the scientific studies and experiments,<b> </b> in the following manner:</p><p class="text-center"><strong>“This study has been conducted using E.U. Copernicus Marine Service Information; </strong>insert all relevant <strong>DOIs links here”</strong></p><p class="text-justify"><strong>2.5</strong> The Licensee will and will procure that its staff, students, contractors and agents abide by the terms and conditions of this Licence.</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>2.6</strong> The Licensee will and will procure that its staff, students, contractors, agents and customers maintain such records to document and trace use of&nbsp;Copernicus Marine Service Products. The Licensee will make such records available to the Copernicus Marine Service upon reasonable&nbsp;notice being given. This requirement will be propagated in all descending licences.</p><h2><em><strong>3. Intellectual Property Rights</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify"><strong>3.1</strong> All Intellectual Property Rights in the Copernicus Marine Service Products belong, and will continue to belong, to the European Union.</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>3.2 </strong>All new Intellectual Property Rights created as a result of modifying or adapting the Copernicus Marine Service Products will be owned by the&nbsp;Licensee.</p><h2><em><strong>4. Disclaimers</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify"><strong>4.1</strong> MERCATOR OCEAN ADVISES THE LICENSEE THAT COPERNICUS MARINE SERVICE PRODUCTS AND INFORMATION ARE PROVIDED WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTY AS REGARDS THEIR QUALITY, ACCURACY, AVAILABILITY, RELIABILITY, SPEED AND SUITABILITY FOR ANY PURPOSE.</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>4.2 </strong>MERCATOR OCEAN EXCLUDES ALL OTHER WARRANTIES, CONDITIONS, TERMS, UNDERTAKINGS, OBLIGATIONS WHETHER&nbsp;EXPRESS OR IMPLIED BY STATUTE INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF SATISFACTORY QUALITY&nbsp;AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE OR OTHERWISE TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.</p><h2><em><strong>5. Liabilities</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify"><strong>5.1</strong> MERCATOR OCEAN will not be held liable for any damage, loss whether direct, indirect or consequential resulting from the Licensee’s use&nbsp;of the Copernicus Marine Service Products.</p><h2><em><strong>6. Breach of this Licence</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify"><strong>6.1</strong> When MERCATOR OCEAN considers that a breach of this Licence has occurred, it may at its discretion take such action as deemed appropriate.<br>Failure to comply with the terms and conditions of the Licence Permissions constitutes a material breach of the terms of use for which&nbsp;the Licensee is permitted to use the Copernicus Marine Service Products and may result in the Copernicus Marine Service taking all or&nbsp;any of the following actions.</p><p class="text-justify">(a) Immediate, temporary or permanent withdrawal of the Licensee’s right to use the Copernicus Marine Service Products.</p><p class="text-justify">(b) Issue a warning to the Licensee.</p><p class="text-justify">(c) Legal proceedings against the Licensee for reimbursement of all costs on an indemnity basis (including but not limited to&nbsp;reasonable administrative and legal costs) resulting from the breach.</p><p class="text-justify">(d) Disclosure of such information to law enforcement authorities as the MERCATOR OCEAN feels is necessary or as required by law.</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>6.2</strong> MERCATOR OCEAN excludes its liability for all action it may take in response to breaches of this Licence. The actions described above are not&nbsp;limited, and MERCATOR OCEAN may take any other action it deems appropriate.</p><p class="text-justify"><strong>6.3 </strong>The Licensee will indemnify MERCATOR OCEAN against breach of this Licence.</p><h2><em><strong>7. Governing Law</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify"><strong>7.1</strong> This Licence will be construed and enforced in accordance with French Law will have exclusive jurisdiction to deal with any dispute that arises&nbsp;out of or in connection with this Licence.</p><h2><em><strong>8. Changes to this Licence</strong></em></h2><p class="text-justify"><strong>8.1</strong> The Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service may revise this Licence at any time.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="spacer__twenty"></div></article></div></div></main><footer role="contentinfo" class="ccl-footer"><div class="ccl-footer-main"><div class="ccl-footer-logo"><div id="block-footer-logo-top" data-block-plugin-id="block_content:7368148c-9103-4667-87c2-dd6f4ad83559" class="settings-tray-editable block block-block-content block-block-content7368148c-9103-4667-87c2-dd6f4ad83559" data-drupal-settingstray="editable"><div class="field field--body field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"><img data-entity-uuid="be74d67e-31a3-4ab9-aad1-77db0a254172" data-entity-type="file" src="/sites/default/files/inline-images/eu-copernicus-copernicusmarine-implementedmercatorocean-white.svg" width="1477" height="185" loading="lazy"></div></div></div><div class="ccl-container ccl-container-flex"><div class="ccl-footer-col"><div class="region region--footer_col1 region-footer-col1"> <nav role="navigation" aria-labelledby="block-footer-menu-follow-us-menu" id="block-footer-menu-follow-us" data-block-plugin-id="system_menu_block:footer-menu-follow-us-section" class="ccl-border-bottom settings-tray-editable block nav nav--footer-menu-follow-us-section block-menu navigation menu--footer-menu-follow-us-section c